Cloud & DevOps Lab — Weeks 6–10

Week 6: Maven

Aim: Build a Java project using Maven.

java -version
mvn -version
cd ~/project-maven
cat pom.xml
cat src/main/java/com/example/App.java
mvn compile
mvn package
ls -lh target/
java -cp target/classes com.example.App

Result to show: "BUILD SUCCESS", generated JAR file, and Java program output.

Week 7: Jenkins

Aim: Install Jenkins and execute a build job.

sudo systemctl start jenkins
sudo systemctl status jenkins
java -version
mvn -version

Browser: Open "http://YOUR-EC2-PUBLIC-IP:8080/" → "jenkins1" → Build Now → Console Output.

Result to show: "Finished: SUCCESS".

Week 8: Docker

Aim: Install Docker and run a container.

docker --version
sudo systemctl start docker
sudo systemctl status docker
sudo docker run hello-world
sudo docker images
sudo docker ps -a
sudo docker info

Result to show: "Hello from Docker!", the image listing, and the container status.

Week 9: AWS ECR

Aim: Build a Docker image and push it to Amazon ECR.

cd ~/week9
cat Dockerfile
sudo docker build -t week9-repo .
sudo docker tag week9-repo:latest 879343933306.dkr.ecr.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/week9-repo:latest
aws ecr get-login-password --region ap-south-1 | sudo docker login --username AWS --password-stdin 879343933306.dkr.ecr.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com
sudo docker push 879343933306.dkr.ecr.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/week9-repo:latest
sudo docker images

Result to show: AWS Console → ECR → "week9-repo" → Images → "latest".

Week 10: AWS CodeCommit

Aim: Use Git to commit, push, branch, and merge code.

cd ~/my-webapp
git status
git log --oneline
git branch -a
git checkout master
git pull
cat index.html
git status

Result to show: Commit history, branches, merged pull request, and "Congratulations V3" in "index.html".

